From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: host: mediatek: skip the HS-G5 sync length on older devices

ufs_mtk_adjust_sync_length() reads and sets PA_TXHSG5SYNCLENGTH on every
device. A UFS 3.1 device rejects it. On a Lenovo TB375FC with a Micron
MT128GBCAV2U31 the peer get and the peer set each fail after three tries
and log an error on every boot. On 7.2.12 the retries also hit the
WARN_ON_ONCE() in ufshcd_dispatch_uic_cmd(), which mainline has since fixed
in the retry loop.

Stop before the gear 5 attribute on devices older than UFS 4.0, which can't
use that gear.
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-mediatek.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-mediatek.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-mediatek.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-mediatek.c
@@ -1388,6 +1388,10 @@
 	};
 
 	cnt = sizeof(pa_min_sync_length) / sizeof(struct attr_min);
+	/* HS-G5 came with UFS 4.0. An older device rejects the attribute. */
+	if (hba->dev_info.wspecversion < 0x0400)
+		cnt--;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < cnt; i++) {
 		att = pa_min_sync_length[i].attr;
 		min = pa_min_sync_length[i].min_value;
